Authorship
----------
  Alvin Sun <sk.alvin.x@gmail.com>   platform, silicon packages, driver, bring-up

The code in this repository was written with AI assistance inside an
interactive session, and every functional change was built and then tested on
a Radxa Cubie A7A: flashed, booted, and measured (sampling-window sweeps are
judged on the data each tap returns, throughputs are measured on the board,
and every speed mode has a revert path).  Claims in commit messages are the
measurements that were taken, not estimates.

Contributing
------------
  - Licence: BSD-2-Clause-Patent (see LICENSE).  By contributing you agree to
    license your contribution under it.
  - Sign-off: every commit needs `Signed-off-by: Your Name <you@example.com>`,
    certifying the Developer Certificate of Origin (DCO 1.1).  Use a real
    identity; placeholder or localhost addresses are rejected.
  - Style: EDK2 coding style, 2-space indent, 80 columns, `EFI_STATUS`
    returns, SPDX header in every new file.
  - Testing: hardware behaviour must be measured, not assumed.  For anything
    touching the storage path, state which mode was negotiated, what the
    sample/strobe taps were, and what the read-back showed.
  - Provenance: do not paste code from GPL sources or from vendor trees into
    this repository.  If you must reference vendor behaviour, describe the
    requirement and implement it independently; see NOTICE.